N2  - Introduction: High levels of social physique anxiety (SPA) can lead to social isolation, mental health disorders, and reduced physical activity participation, especially in women with obesity. Psychological intervention developed to address SPA in this population are lacking. This randomized controlled trial aimed to 1) assess the feasibility and acceptability of the study protocol and a psychological intervention with virtual reality exposure and exercise training, and 2) explore the effects of this intervention on SPA, body appreciation (BA) and weight bias internalisation (WBI). Method(s): Forty-five participants (Mage=39.3+/-5.7 years; MBMI=40.2+/- 5.3 kg/m2) were randomly assigned to one of three groups: 1) ET+VR (exercise training + psychological intervention with cognitive restructuring.
